healthy baby.


01:32:46.742 --> 01:32:48.742
-Wow.
-Yes, chubsters.


01:32:48.825 --> 01:32:49.992
Mm-hmm.


01:32:50.076 --> 01:32:52.159
We got the electroencephalogram,
EEG.


01:32:52.242 --> 01:32:55.742
We didn't see any
abnormal electrical activity


01:32:55.825 --> 01:32:58.408
that would tell us there's
a part of her brain


01:32:58.493 --> 01:33:01.785
that is at risk for generating
more seizures,


01:33:01.868 --> 01:33:06.534
but the EEG measured
45 minutes in her life.


01:33:06.618 --> 01:33:09.244
Now,
it's been another three months.


01:33:09.369 --> 01:33:11.119
Um, she's five months old now,


01:33:11.203 --> 01:33:13.703
and you're not noticing
anything concerning,


01:33:13.787 --> 01:33:15.411
so that is exceptional.


01:33:17.204 --> 01:33:20.287
I have no evidence that
cocaine exposure


01:33:20.370 --> 01:33:23.162
caused a seizure or--
or injured her brain


01:33:23.245 --> 01:33:27.829
in a fashion which would explain
the seizure that she had.


01:33:27.913 --> 01:33:33.122
When we look at the best studies
of infants exposed to cocaine,


01:33:33.206 --> 01:33:34.872
methamphetamine, amphetamines,


01:33:34.955 --> 01:33:40.290
the main thing we worry about is
long-term developmental issues,


01:33:40.373 --> 01:33:43.373
and it's something
only time can tell.


01:33:43.456 --> 01:33:47.123
Every day, every week,
every month that passes by,


01:33:47.207 --> 01:33:49.956
